{# Interactive money mechanics. Each one answers a question you can feel the
   answer to by dragging something, which is the point: a number that moves
   while you move beats three paragraphs you skim. #}
<div id="pane-explain" hidden>
  <div class="filters">
    <span class="stamp">Drag the controls. The numbers update as you move.</span>
    <span class="stamp" id="xp-featured-note"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="compound" data-tracks="time investing psychology">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">Why saving feels pointless for two years, then doesn't</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">Compounding pays almost nothing early and almost everything late. That shape is the whole reason patience is hard — the feedback arrives last.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Monthly amount<input type="range" id="c-amt" min="5000" max="100000" step="5000" value="20000"><output id="c-amt-o"></output></label>
        <label>Annual return<input type="range" id="c-ret" min="0" max="12" step="0.5" value="5"><output id="c-ret-o"></output></label>
        <label>Years<input type="range" id="c-yrs" min="1" max="40" step="1" value="20"><output id="c-yrs-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="c-total">—</span><span class="hero-l">total after <span id="c-yrs-l">20</span> years</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split">
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-1)"></i>You put in <b id="c-in">—</b></span>
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-2)"></i>Growth added <b id="c-gain">—</b></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="c-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="c-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="c-cap">Total balance against the money you actually contributed.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="c-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="inflation" data-tracks="intelligence history time">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">What your cash quietly loses</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">Money sitting still shrinks. Rome did this deliberately by removing silver from the denarius; modern inflation does it without anyone deciding.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Starting amount<input type="range" id="i-amt" min="100000" max="10000000" step="100000" value="1000000"><output id="i-amt-o"></output></label>
        <label>Inflation<input type="range" id="i-rate" min="0" max="10" step="0.1" value="2"><output id="i-rate-o"></output></label>
        <label>Years<input type="range" id="i-yrs" min="1" max="40" step="1" value="20"><output id="i-yrs-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="i-val">—</span><span class="hero-l">what it still buys</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split"><span>Lost to inflation <b id="i-lost">—</b></span></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="i-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="i-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="i-cap">Purchasing power of the same nominal amount over time.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="i-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="leverage" data-tracks="markets crypto financing">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">What borrowing does to being wrong</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">Leverage multiplies the move, not the odds. The same multiple that doubles a gain doubles the loss — and a big enough loss ends the game.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Your own money<input type="range" id="l-eq" min="100000" max="5000000" step="100000" value="1000000"><output id="l-eq-o"></output></label>
        <label>Leverage<input type="range" id="l-x" min="1" max="10" step="0.5" value="3"><output id="l-x-o"></output></label>
        <label>Asset moves<input type="range" id="l-mv" min="-50" max="50" step="1" value="10"><output id="l-mv-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="l-res">—</span><span class="hero-l" id="l-res-l">your money afterwards</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split"><span>Return on your money <b id="l-pct">—</b></span></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="l-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="l-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="l-cap">Your outcome at this leverage across the range of possible moves.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="l-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="cash" data-tracks="financing management">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">How a profitable business runs out of money</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">Profit is an opinion about timing; cash is a fact. You pay costs now and get paid later, so the faster you grow the deeper the hole goes first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Monthly sales growth<input type="range" id="k-g" min="0" max="40" step="1" value="15"><output id="k-g-o"></output></label>
        <label>Clients pay after<input type="range" id="k-d" min="0" max="120" step="5" value="60"><output id="k-d-o"></output></label>
        <label>Gross margin<input type="range" id="k-m" min="10" max="90" step="5" value="50"><output id="k-m-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="k-low">—</span><span class="hero-l">deepest cash hole</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split">
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-1)"></i>Cumulative profit <b id="k-prof">—</b></span>
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-3)"></i>Cash in the bank <b id="k-cash">—</b></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="k-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="k-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="k-cap">Cumulative profit against actual cash, over 24 months.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="k-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="drawdown" data-tracks="time psychology investing">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">How long a loss takes to undo</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">A 50% fall needs a 100% gain to get back to even. Depth is what people fear; duration is what actually makes them quit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>The fall<input type="range" id="d-loss" min="5" max="80" step="5" value="40"><output id="d-loss-o"></output></label>
        <label>Return after<input type="range" id="d-ret" min="1" max="15" step="0.5" value="7"><output id="d-ret-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="d-yrs">—</span><span class="hero-l">years just to get back to where you started</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split"><span>Gain required <b id="d-need">—</b></span></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="d-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="d-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="d-cap">Value over time: the fall, then the climb back to the starting line.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="d-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="timerate" data-tracks="time investing">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">Time beats rate, and it is not close</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">Everyone hunts a better return. Almost nobody extends the horizon, which is the lever that actually moves the number — and the only one fully in your control.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Patient return<input type="range" id="t-r1" min="1" max="12" step="0.5" value="5"><output id="t-r1-o"></output></label>
        <label>Patient years<input type="range" id="t-y1" min="5" max="40" step="1" value="30"><output id="t-y1-o"></output></label>
        <label>Impatient return<input type="range" id="t-r2" min="1" max="30" step="0.5" value="12"><output id="t-r2-o"></output></label>
        <label>Impatient years<input type="range" id="t-y2" min="1" max="40" step="1" value="10"><output id="t-y2-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="t-win">—</span><span class="hero-l" id="t-win-l"></span></div>
        <div class="hero-split">
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-1)"></i>Patient <b id="t-v1">—</b></span>
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-2)"></i>Impatient <b id="t-v2">—</b></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="t-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="t-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="t-cap">Same ¥20,000 a month, two different horizons.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="t-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="checking" data-tracks="time psychology markets">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">The cost of looking</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">The more often you check, the more losses you see — and the less risk you can stomach holding. The asset did not change; your sampling rate did.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Expected return<input type="range" id="k2-r" min="0" max="12" step="0.5" value="7"><output id="k2-r-o"></output></label>
        <label>Volatility<input type="range" id="k2-v" min="5" max="40" step="1" value="18"><output id="k2-v-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="k2-day">—</span><span class="hero-l">chance of a loss if you check daily</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split"><span>Checking once a year <b id="k2-yr">—</b></span><span>Once a decade <b id="k2-dec">—</b></span></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="k2-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="k2-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="k2-cap">Probability of seeing a loss, by how often you look.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="k2-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="xp" data-xp="fees" data-tracks="investing markets time">
    <div class="xp-head">
      <h3 class="xp-title">What 1% a year actually takes</h3>
      <p class="xp-sub">A fee sounds like a rounding error because it is quoted annually. Over a working life it compounds against you exactly as returns compound for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="xp-body">
      <div class="xp-controls">
        <label>Annual fee<input type="range" id="f-fee" min="0" max="3" step="0.05" value="1"><output id="f-fee-o"></output></label>
        <label>Gross return<input type="range" id="f-ret" min="1" max="12" step="0.5" value="6"><output id="f-ret-o"></output></label>
        <label>Years<input type="range" id="f-yrs" min="5" max="45" step="1" value="35"><output id="f-yrs-o"></output></label>
      </div>
      <div class="xp-out">
        <div class="hero"><span class="hero-n" id="f-lost">—</span><span class="hero-l">of your final balance goes to fees</span></div>
        <div class="hero-split">
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-1)"></i>You keep <b id="f-keep">—</b></span>
          <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--viz-2)"></i>They take <b id="f-take">—</b></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="xp-fig"><svg id="f-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="f-cap"></svg>
        <figcaption id="f-cap">Balance with and without the fee, over time.</figcaption></figure>
      <p class="xp-note" id="f-note"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
